0005-relocation-addends

Relocated fields carry the addend (target offset from its symbol), as the XDK linker expects:
ADDR32 holds it; REFHI holds its high half adjusted for the sign of the low half, which goes in the
following PAIR; REFLO holds the low half; REL24/REL14 hold the addend minus the instruction offset.
Verified against the XDK linker with hand-made objects. Without it, pointers and calls into the
middle of functions (exception tables, funclets) land on the function start.

